# Authenticated client fetch

## Requirement

Do **not** call authenticated same-origin APIs (`/api/me`, `/api/competitions`, admin roster, etc.) via top-level `await` in page or component setup during SSR.

Fetch in **`onMounted`** (or another explicit client-only lifecycle), after **`await hydrateIfNeeded()`** when the route is auth-gated.

## Rationale

During SSR, `$fetch` with `credentials: "include"` does not attach the browser session to Nitro’s internal request. Only session bootstrap forwards cookies (see `useAuthUser.fetchSession`). Top-level setup fetches therefore return **401** on refresh and can show spurious toasts or empty state.

## Initial load errors

Prefer **inline page error state** for the first fetch failure. Reserve **toasts** for user-triggered mutations (save, delete, etc.).

## Exception

Session bootstrap uses cookie forwarding in [`app/composables/useAuthUser.ts`](app/composables/useAuthUser.ts). Do not duplicate that pattern ad hoc for other endpoints unless there is a deliberate SSR requirement (e.g. SEO or no-JS first paint).

## Reference implementations

- [`app/pages/competitions/index.vue`](app/pages/competitions/index.vue) — `onMounted` → `hydrateIfNeeded` → fetch; inline `errorMessage`
- [`app/pages/settings/index.vue`](app/pages/settings/index.vue) — same pattern for `GET /api/me`
- [`app/components/admin/MemberManagement.vue`](app/components/admin/MemberManagement.vue) — `onMounted` → `loadRoster`

## Example

```typescript
// ❌ Avoid — runs on SSR without session cookies
await loadProfile();

// ✅ Prefer
onMounted(async () => {
  await hydrateIfNeeded();
  await loadProfile();
});
```
